1
00:00:10,640 --> 00:00:13,159
LONPUR

2
00:00:24,463 --> 00:00:25,690
Good morning.

3
00:00:27,810 --> 00:00:29,183
Tell me something swamiji.

4
00:00:29,610 --> 00:00:31,877
You're such a good
detective and yet

5
00:00:32,177 --> 00:00:34,930
you don't charge money
after solving the case

6
00:00:35,343 --> 00:00:37,263
nor do you take
credit for it in the news.

7
00:00:37,360 --> 00:00:39,776
So you want me to charge
money to find goats? No, no, no...

8
00:00:40,623 --> 00:00:42,669
That would be against
mine and the goat's pride.

9
00:00:42,810 --> 00:00:44,696
Besides, taaka maati, maati taaka.

10
00:00:44,696 --> 00:00:45,976
Taka taki maka maki? What?

11
00:00:45,976 --> 00:00:47,756
Money is like sand.

12
00:00:48,463 --> 00:00:49,813
Ramakrishna Paramahansa.

13
00:00:49,827 --> 00:00:51,617
Don't you know that
Mr. Ashram visitor?

14
00:00:51,883 --> 00:00:54,070
-Good morning.
-Good morning Mrs. H.

15
00:00:54,657 --> 00:00:55,756
Did you hear?

16
00:00:55,781 --> 00:01:00,210
Swamiji has proclaimed
today that money is like sand.

17
00:01:00,317 --> 00:01:04,190
So I think we should start paying
our rent to Mrs. H with a box of sand.

18
00:01:04,800 --> 00:01:07,077
I will throw that sand
back in your faces.

19
00:01:07,102 --> 00:01:09,303
No need for tension Henry.
He has a pension.

20
00:01:09,330 --> 00:01:12,210
-A pension isn't enough these days.
-You also have a permanent job.

21
00:01:12,330 --> 00:01:13,803
-You are my assistant.
-Hello?

22
00:01:14,190 --> 00:01:16,170
Not assistant okay. Partner.

23
00:01:16,517 --> 00:01:20,335
I thought that we should start
our own detective agency.

24
00:01:20,360 --> 00:01:21,920
To solve cases and make money.

25
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:24,360
-That's a great idea.
-No, no, no.

26
00:01:24,570 --> 00:01:25,817
See Mrs. H?

27
00:01:25,950 --> 00:01:28,263
He might be a talented man
but he is also very selfish.

28
00:01:28,320 --> 00:01:29,483
No, no, no.

29
00:01:29,483 --> 00:01:31,443
If not about yourself,
at least think about others.

30
00:01:31,468 --> 00:01:33,370
-No. No.
-Think about Mrs. H.

31
00:01:33,395 --> 00:01:35,455
-I am all alone Shekhar.
-Yeah.

32
00:01:35,480 --> 00:01:37,280
Your rent would really
help me, you know?

33
00:01:37,290 --> 00:01:38,723
Yeah, she needs the money.

34
00:01:39,697 --> 00:01:40,730
What do you say?

35
00:01:45,397 --> 00:01:46,583
One...

36
00:01:47,370 --> 00:01:50,910
One week. We can try it
out for one week.

37
00:01:50,977 --> 00:01:52,132
Yes!

38
00:01:52,157 --> 00:01:55,296
-Yes, but I will handle the money.
-Absolutely.

39
00:01:55,610 --> 00:01:57,223
What should we name our agency?

40
00:01:57,310 --> 00:01:59,390
Saini and Home detective agency?

41
00:01:59,583 --> 00:02:03,010
How about, 'Saini, Home
and Henry associates'?

42
00:02:03,257 --> 00:02:05,797
Oh! Then why don't
we include Pintu also?

43
00:02:05,883 --> 00:02:09,543
Saini, Home, Henry and Pintu
will become... SHHP...

44
00:02:09,568 --> 00:02:12,690
I think it's Henry and Saini...
That will be...

45
00:02:15,717 --> 00:02:16,757
Well done!

46
00:02:23,877 --> 00:02:26,996
I have been seeing
ghosts for the last few days.

47
00:02:27,537 --> 00:02:29,170
That is not a ghost,
that is Jayavrat.

48
00:02:30,470 --> 00:02:34,370
She received a family gold chain
on her 18th birthday from dad.

49
00:02:34,483 --> 00:02:37,075
But when we opened the
box to wear it for the wedding

50
00:02:37,099 --> 00:02:38,790
last night the chain was missing.

51
00:02:40,880 --> 00:02:44,116
Mr. Shekhar I wrote a story last
night that was 15 pages long.

52
00:02:45,043 --> 00:02:47,283
When I woke up in the morning
three pages were missing.

53
00:02:50,280 --> 00:02:53,880
Don't worry, he is very good
at ending the story.

54
00:02:54,277 --> 00:02:56,870
Don't worry, he knows how to
talk to ghosts.

55
00:02:57,363 --> 00:02:59,930
You just need to pay the fees.
100 rupees.

56
00:03:00,360 --> 00:03:02,480
50 rupees only.
You just need to pay us.

57
00:03:02,495 --> 00:03:03,950
No... he is a student.

58
00:03:04,350 --> 00:03:05,815
-Oh, are you a student?
-Yes.

59
00:03:05,840 --> 00:03:09,320
Then you get a 50% student discount.
50 rupees only.

60
00:03:17,743 --> 00:03:19,270
100 rupees only.

61
00:03:20,070 --> 00:03:22,563
He is such a bad doctor!
He is asking for money from a cop?

62
00:03:23,010 --> 00:03:24,270
The cops should...

63
00:03:24,630 --> 00:03:25,756
No...

64
00:03:26,840 --> 00:03:28,167
Well, okay...

65
00:04:01,917 --> 00:04:03,137
Goswami...

66
00:04:04,083 --> 00:04:05,537
I don't feel good.

67
00:04:06,623 --> 00:04:07,770
Why?

68
00:04:08,670 --> 00:04:11,623
Because Das isn't here.
He always sets a good mood.

69
00:04:12,737 --> 00:04:14,623
He must be attending a wedding.

70
00:04:15,480 --> 00:04:17,040
Since he is unable to get
married himself.

71
00:04:17,077 --> 00:04:18,590
Hey, that is a good thing.

72
00:04:18,650 --> 00:04:21,017
Otherwise he would go from
Das to sad.

73
00:04:21,560 --> 00:04:23,820
-Just like us.
-Should I tell your wife that?

74
00:04:24,020 --> 00:04:25,833
Hey, Goswami...

75
00:04:26,880 --> 00:04:29,447
-Here. You eat.
-Sad huh?

76
00:04:29,530 --> 00:04:31,017
From Chatterjee to sad.

77
00:04:31,017 --> 00:04:32,210
From Das to sad.

78
00:04:39,717 --> 00:04:40,937
Good morning.

79
00:04:42,357 --> 00:04:43,570
Good morning Das.

80
00:04:44,323 --> 00:04:45,930
Good morning Das?

81
00:04:47,337 --> 00:04:48,676
Das?

82
00:04:49,809 --> 00:04:51,289
Good morning.

83
00:04:51,983 --> 00:04:55,463
Mr. Shekhar, I was sitting in
my store like I generally do...

84
00:04:55,483 --> 00:04:56,896
And looking at matrimonial ads.

85
00:04:57,080 --> 00:04:59,206
-What?
-Everyone in Lonpur knows

86
00:04:59,206 --> 00:05:01,510
what you do in your shop.

87
00:05:01,920 --> 00:05:05,040
Which ads you cross out and which
ones you circle. Please go on.

88
00:05:05,143 --> 00:05:06,597
What else can I do Shekhar?

89
00:05:07,560 --> 00:05:10,340
A good girl is like the view
from Kangchenjunga.

90
00:05:10,843 --> 00:05:13,377
It's not easy.
You need to work hard for it.

91
00:05:13,880 --> 00:05:16,680
So, did you find a girl Mr. Das?

92
00:05:16,917 --> 00:05:18,050
I found a flyer.

93
00:05:18,583 --> 00:05:20,617
I found a flyer in the newspaper

94
00:05:21,217 --> 00:05:23,143
that had an ad
looking for a groom.

95
00:05:23,397 --> 00:05:26,576
It said that the girl
has four conditions.

96
00:05:26,763 --> 00:05:27,863
Interesting.

97
00:05:28,130 --> 00:05:30,130
The boy that she wants...

98
00:05:30,155 --> 00:05:32,237
You mean 'man', right?

99
00:05:34,717 --> 00:05:36,983
A man above the age of 40.

100
00:05:37,600 --> 00:05:42,333
A Bengali whose
surname starts with D...

101
00:05:42,863 --> 00:05:44,223
and who runs their own business.

102
00:05:44,417 --> 00:05:46,783
So I fulfilled all four of them.

103
00:05:48,657 --> 00:05:50,763
I even met the girl's father,

104
00:05:50,943 --> 00:05:52,223
Shottendra Sanyal.

105
00:05:52,657 --> 00:05:55,336
He was a very good man.
A complete gentleman.

106
00:05:55,695 --> 00:05:56,677
He even said -

107
00:05:56,720 --> 00:05:59,660
I can't believe my luck.

108
00:06:00,070 --> 00:06:02,463
You have all four qualities.

109
00:06:05,157 --> 00:06:08,883
You would be absolutely perfect
for my daughter Menaka.

110
00:06:08,950 --> 00:06:10,117
Absolutely perfect.

111
00:06:10,997 --> 00:06:12,277
Thank you sir. Er...

112
00:06:13,643 --> 00:06:14,937
Papa.

113
00:06:14,970 --> 00:06:18,297
It looks like we will all have to

114
00:06:18,617 --> 00:06:21,257
prepare for your welcome
son-in-law.

115
00:06:24,510 --> 00:06:26,703
But there is one small problem.

116
00:06:26,990 --> 00:06:29,423
My daughter is a forest officer.

117
00:06:30,330 --> 00:06:33,123
She wants a life partner

118
00:06:33,463 --> 00:06:37,016
who would be willing to
move out of the city

119
00:06:37,080 --> 00:06:40,200
and live in a forest if necessary.

120
00:06:43,120 --> 00:06:45,200
Of course I am
willing to do that.

121
00:06:45,590 --> 00:06:46,643
We will see.

122
00:06:47,123 --> 00:06:51,730
If you live in this jungle
and survive for 30 days

123
00:06:52,870 --> 00:06:56,257
then on the 31st day you
can marry Menaka.

124
00:06:57,210 --> 00:06:59,683
Live in a jungle for a month?
All alone?

125
00:06:59,983 --> 00:07:03,677
I had to prove that I could
live in the jungle for 30 days.

126
00:07:04,477 --> 00:07:08,270
For Menaka I had to become
the sage Vishvamitra.

127
00:07:08,683 --> 00:07:13,316
I sacrificed my house, my shop
and everything for her.

128
00:07:14,783 --> 00:07:15,869
Dad...

129
00:07:16,210 --> 00:07:18,077
I mean, Mr. Sanyal...

130
00:07:18,370 --> 00:07:20,243
would give me a task every day

131
00:07:20,270 --> 00:07:23,090
and I would put all my effort into
completing the task.

132
00:07:23,970 --> 00:07:25,523
DAY ONE

133
00:07:30,737 --> 00:07:32,363
DAY SIX

134
00:07:32,830 --> 00:07:37,536
Menaka's condition was to
fulfill every single day's task

135
00:07:37,630 --> 00:07:40,695
if I skipped even a single task
then I would have to restart.

136
00:07:40,720 --> 00:07:43,080
DAY THIRTEEN

137
00:07:43,750 --> 00:07:46,256
But Mr. Sanyal
didn't show up today.

138
00:07:47,597 --> 00:07:48,658
DAY TWENTY

139
00:07:48,683 --> 00:07:50,657
I waited for a very long time.

140
00:07:51,560 --> 00:07:54,200
When I enquired from the
forest rangers, they told me…

141
00:07:54,217 --> 00:07:56,423
That there is no forest
officer named Menaka.

142
00:07:57,117 --> 00:07:59,610
And nobody knows anyone by the
name of Sanyal either.

143
00:07:59,970 --> 00:08:00,970
Ouch.

144
00:08:02,043 --> 00:08:05,897
Shekhar, I have
completed 20 days out of 30.

145
00:08:06,290 --> 00:08:07,943
There are only 10 days remaining.

146
00:08:08,510 --> 00:08:10,003
If I stop now...

147
00:08:10,330 --> 00:08:13,137
I will turn into a widow
before I even got married.

148
00:08:13,230 --> 00:08:14,570
-Widower.
-What?

149
00:08:14,957 --> 00:08:17,730
Not a 'widow', you would be a
'widower' since you are a man.

150
00:08:18,480 --> 00:08:20,720
So you want me to find Sanyal?

151
00:08:20,777 --> 00:08:21,843
That's right.

152
00:08:24,843 --> 00:08:26,010
Okay then Mr. Das.

153
00:08:26,657 --> 00:08:28,137
1,000 rupees.

154
00:08:28,457 --> 00:08:31,657
500 right now and 500 with
the wedding sweets?

155
00:08:32,197 --> 00:08:35,063
Doctor, my shop has been shut
for the last 20 days.

156
00:08:35,343 --> 00:08:37,463
I don't have any money.

157
00:08:37,877 --> 00:08:40,009
That's fine, you can give me
whatever you have.

158
00:08:40,780 --> 00:08:42,310
-You can give it later.
-Shekhar!

159
00:08:42,310 --> 00:08:44,230
-How could you do that?
-He doesn't have any money.

160
00:08:44,230 --> 00:08:46,223
-This is my department.
-This is my company.

161
00:08:46,240 --> 00:08:47,496
It's our company.

162
00:08:47,760 --> 00:08:48,993
Then it's time to shut down.

163
00:08:49,923 --> 00:08:51,363
Which jungle is it?

164
00:09:41,930 --> 00:09:44,863
Brother, Das and Bhootnath
kyalakeli korche.

165
00:09:44,977 --> 00:09:47,310
-Kala Koli?
-They are fighting! Hurry up!

166
00:09:47,383 --> 00:09:49,343
It’s not about my
house or your house,

167
00:09:49,343 --> 00:09:51,356
why would you do an
illegal construction...

168
00:09:51,381 --> 00:09:53,239
Who says it's illegal? This
is the wall of my house,

169
00:09:53,263 --> 00:09:55,377
I did this construction.
My father was alive when it was built.

170
00:09:55,403 --> 00:09:58,310
It’s not about your
house or my house,

171
00:09:58,457 --> 00:10:01,590
-our houses are facing each other...
-This wall was created by my father!

172
00:10:01,643 --> 00:10:03,723
Did you think I wouldn't
notice, you thief!

173
00:10:03,810 --> 00:10:06,777
How am I the thief? The wall
is exactly where the line was!

174
00:10:07,003 --> 00:10:09,177
You liar! You are a cheat!

175
00:10:09,240 --> 00:10:10,806
-Break the wall. Do it!
-I won't.

176
00:10:10,833 --> 00:10:11,910
Then I will break you.

177
00:10:11,935 --> 00:10:15,610
Hey, hey, why are you fighting?
You might get hurt.

178
00:10:15,917 --> 00:10:17,175
I am not afraid of getting hurt.

179
00:10:17,200 --> 00:10:20,476
I have a balm in my shop.
Crocodile brand balm.

180
00:10:20,850 --> 00:10:23,363
-I will...
-Hey!

181
00:10:31,960 --> 00:10:33,858
You guys don't know
how to use your fists.

182
00:10:34,200 --> 00:10:35,940
Use your words and talk it out.

183
00:10:44,897 --> 00:10:46,283
Where are you going?

184
00:10:47,903 --> 00:10:49,150
To eat lunch.

185
00:10:52,290 --> 00:10:53,357
Who is that?

186
00:10:53,382 --> 00:10:54,783
This is Das' Menaka.

187
00:10:55,430 --> 00:10:56,650
Das and her?

188
00:10:57,190 --> 00:10:59,137
She could be miss universe.

189
00:11:00,063 --> 00:11:02,097
A desperate man like Das
was bound to fall for it.

190
00:11:03,223 --> 00:11:05,236
Yes, because everyone in Lonpur
knows

191
00:11:05,280 --> 00:11:07,680
that Das spends his days
looking at matrimonials.

192
00:11:11,470 --> 00:11:12,630
Show me your hand.

193
00:11:13,237 --> 00:11:15,037
-Why?
-Just do it.

194
00:11:20,703 --> 00:11:22,423
-What is this?
-The key to the company.

195
00:11:24,243 --> 00:11:25,637
It's time to open up again.

196
00:11:27,970 --> 00:11:29,510
-Where are you going?
-What?

197
00:11:29,597 --> 00:11:31,710
Didn't you just say we
we are going out for lunch?

198
00:11:35,880 --> 00:11:37,267
Partner!

199
00:11:39,190 --> 00:11:41,330
So, we already know what Das wants.

200
00:11:42,690 --> 00:11:44,557
Now tell me what Sanyal wants.

201
00:11:46,090 --> 00:11:47,370
You know what I think?

202
00:11:47,450 --> 00:11:49,816
I think Sanyal was
sent by Bhoothnath.

203
00:11:50,037 --> 00:11:51,243
Das' cousin brother.

204
00:11:51,720 --> 00:11:54,650
Bhootnath and Das have been
enemies for a very long time

205
00:11:54,675 --> 00:11:56,523
because of a dispute
over land they inherited.

206
00:11:57,023 --> 00:11:58,710
Bhoothnath must have sent Sanyal

207
00:11:58,743 --> 00:12:01,483
to send Das into the jungle

208
00:12:01,677 --> 00:12:05,110
while Bhootnath broke the
old wall and built a new one.

209
00:12:06,163 --> 00:12:09,010
Game. Set. Match.
Chamionship partner.

210
00:12:09,035 --> 00:12:11,216
Wow, such a terrible deduction.

211
00:12:11,557 --> 00:12:13,976
Wait, wait a minute.
Why? What was so bad about it?

212
00:12:14,583 --> 00:12:18,415
There is a suspect and a motive
and I even investigated it myself.

213
00:12:18,440 --> 00:12:22,083
I saw them fighting about the
land and the position of the wall.

214
00:12:22,437 --> 00:12:23,550
-Really?
-Yes!

215
00:12:24,177 --> 00:12:26,590
So, how long does it take
to build a wall?

216
00:12:27,123 --> 00:12:29,317
To build... It probably
takes two days.

217
00:12:30,090 --> 00:12:32,677
And for how long was
Mr. Das sent to the jungle?

218
00:12:33,430 --> 00:12:34,623
For 30 days.

219
00:12:35,790 --> 00:12:36,830
Huh?

220
00:12:44,323 --> 00:12:45,543
Afternoon Henry.

221
00:12:45,568 --> 00:12:46,570
Good afternoon.

222
00:12:46,863 --> 00:12:48,930
-Good afternoon Mrs. H.
-Good afternoon.

223
00:12:48,955 --> 00:12:50,097
Two specials for us please.

224
00:12:50,137 --> 00:12:51,477
Namaste sister-in-law.

225
00:12:51,670 --> 00:12:52,690
Laltoo!

226
00:12:54,057 --> 00:12:55,310
Hello.

227
00:12:55,643 --> 00:12:57,250
So... I see you're eating
Kosha Mangsho.

228
00:12:57,320 --> 00:13:00,213
Of course, a Sunday holiday

229
00:13:00,373 --> 00:13:02,819
is all about enjoying
time and Mangsho with my family.

230
00:13:02,723 --> 00:13:05,463
A cop taking a holiday means
they have solved all their cases.

231
00:13:05,517 --> 00:13:07,463
-Just like our Jayavrat.
-Hey!

232
00:13:07,650 --> 00:13:09,937
- Conceited man.
-Good joke. Good joke.

233
00:13:10,217 --> 00:13:13,377
So, what case are you guys
working on right now?

234
00:13:13,943 --> 00:13:16,063
Das. Abhirup Das.

235
00:13:17,743 --> 00:13:20,617
No way. That good-for-nothing Das?

236
00:13:20,977 --> 00:13:25,090
Shekhar, will you work
for anyone who pays you?

237
00:13:25,950 --> 00:13:28,003
You have lost your soul
to capitalism my friend.

238
00:13:28,063 --> 00:13:29,543
He is the capitalist. Not me.

239
00:13:29,777 --> 00:13:31,010
What do you mean capitalist?

240
00:13:31,035 --> 00:13:34,097
Our Karl Marx from Lonpur over here
is helping the poor guy for free?

241
00:13:34,157 --> 00:13:36,670
Who is a poor guy?
That guy is a complete...

242
00:13:37,463 --> 00:13:38,943
Good boy.

243
00:13:39,337 --> 00:13:40,570
Don't move your hands.

244
00:13:41,023 --> 00:13:42,163
Don't try to listen.

245
00:13:45,090 --> 00:13:46,663
He is a complete bastard.

246
00:13:47,377 --> 00:13:49,377
Do you know Urmila from
the chemist shop?

247
00:13:49,843 --> 00:13:52,670
He was desperate
to get married to her.

248
00:13:52,840 --> 00:13:55,320
But he caused a huge scene.
She complained against him

249
00:13:55,361 --> 00:13:57,070
and I beat him
away with my stick.

250
00:13:57,150 --> 00:14:00,003
But he still didn't stop.
Do you know what he did?

251
00:14:00,177 --> 00:14:03,097
He cut his wrists and wrote
the girl a letter with his blood.

252
00:14:03,280 --> 00:14:05,080
And he didn't even get a
government stamp.

253
00:14:05,137 --> 00:14:07,103
Poor guy? Bloody bastard.

254
00:14:11,457 --> 00:14:13,030
My son...

255
00:14:13,617 --> 00:14:14,730
So partner?

256
00:14:15,777 --> 00:14:17,543
Urmila who works
at the medical store.

257
00:14:17,970 --> 00:14:19,530
Let's go meet her.

258
00:14:19,623 --> 00:14:21,590
-Let's have lunch first.
-You can eat later.

259
00:14:21,930 --> 00:14:22,895
But...

260
00:14:22,920 --> 00:14:24,983
No, just go. Go.
You have to go.

261
00:14:25,560 --> 00:14:26,960
Both of you.

262
00:14:28,120 --> 00:14:30,207
-Come on!
-Okay...

263
00:14:38,170 --> 00:14:40,697
-Give this to Abra uncle.
-Okay sir.

264
00:14:40,737 --> 00:14:42,637
Oh and take this too.

265
00:14:42,763 --> 00:14:45,037
Give it to Abra uncle. Quickly.

266
00:14:45,183 --> 00:14:46,477
Oh Shekhar!

267
00:14:47,250 --> 00:14:48,450
And Jayabroto is with you too?

268
00:14:48,863 --> 00:14:50,313
-Jayavrat.
-Exactly.

269
00:14:50,333 --> 00:14:52,320
Where is Urmila?
I need to speak to her.

270
00:14:52,320 --> 00:14:54,030
Should I call her? Urmila!

271
00:14:54,877 --> 00:14:55,910
Come out.

272
00:14:57,050 --> 00:14:58,070
He...

273
00:15:00,797 --> 00:15:04,716
Hey wait! Listen. Listen.
Please listen.

274
00:15:04,783 --> 00:15:06,757
-Just listen to me.
-Please.

275
00:15:07,657 --> 00:15:09,150
Please stop following me.

276
00:15:09,280 --> 00:15:11,770
I do not want to marry you.

277
00:15:11,823 --> 00:15:12,883
-Huh?
-What?

278
00:15:13,720 --> 00:15:15,540
Marry? You?

279
00:15:17,650 --> 00:15:18,333
Never.

280
00:15:18,333 --> 00:15:20,656
-So you don't want to get married?
-No, not at all.

281
00:15:20,737 --> 00:15:24,290
Then why do you keep sending Mrs. H
to my house with a proposal?

282
00:15:25,223 --> 00:15:28,463
Last time she brought
flowers and sweets.

283
00:15:29,650 --> 00:15:32,123
You are a weird man.
Acting innocent now.

284
00:15:32,437 --> 00:15:34,877
You like me but you can't
even say it to my face?

285
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:39,320
Sorry.

286
00:15:42,190 --> 00:15:43,957
-Look, I don't want to get married.
-I see.

287
00:15:44,680 --> 00:15:47,372
And... you...
sorry but I definitely don't
want to get married to you.

288
00:15:47,397 --> 00:15:50,156
If you don't want to get married
then why are you following me?

289
00:15:50,350 --> 00:15:53,263
-Because--
-Oh so it's for a case again!

290
00:15:53,690 --> 00:15:55,423
-Again?
-That's right. Again.

291
00:15:56,317 --> 00:15:58,683
Last time Inspector Laha was here

292
00:15:58,857 --> 00:16:02,430
and he informed me that I am
the 'U' Killer's girlfriend.

293
00:16:02,850 --> 00:16:04,010
'U' for Urmila.

294
00:16:04,817 --> 00:16:05,963
That is what he said.

295
00:16:06,363 --> 00:16:08,743
First Das, and then Laha

296
00:16:09,680 --> 00:16:11,826
and now you two.

297
00:16:11,857 --> 00:16:13,797
Have all the men in
town lost their minds?

298
00:16:13,822 --> 00:16:17,057
Is that why you wanted
revenge against Das?

299
00:16:18,377 --> 00:16:20,690
No, no, listen.

300
00:16:20,910 --> 00:16:23,690
I don't even want to look
at Das to get revenge.

301
00:16:26,190 --> 00:16:27,870
-Are you guys done?
-Yes.

302
00:16:28,103 --> 00:16:29,790
-Can I leave?
-Yes. Sorry...

303
00:16:30,063 --> 00:16:31,310
Good.

304
00:16:34,717 --> 00:16:36,863
"Is that why you wanted
revenge against Das?"

305
00:16:37,810 --> 00:16:39,723
You have the subtlety
of a hammer my friend.

306
00:16:40,510 --> 00:16:42,450
What? Me? What about you?

307
00:16:42,683 --> 00:16:45,210
What you said to her?
Is she that bad?

308
00:16:45,243 --> 00:16:46,670
I don't want to get married!

309
00:16:47,440 --> 00:16:49,560
Why don't you and Henry
start a matrimonial together?

310
00:16:51,840 --> 00:16:53,780
Both of you are pushing
me to get married!

311
00:16:53,920 --> 00:16:56,000
You shouldn't be so
adamant about everything...

312
00:16:58,163 --> 00:16:59,490
Urmila was right.

313
00:17:00,637 --> 00:17:02,503
About what? That she is very pretty?

314
00:17:02,777 --> 00:17:05,230
Should I tell Mrs. H
to talk to her again?

315
00:17:05,463 --> 00:17:06,837
Oh! Joke?

316
00:17:08,097 --> 00:17:10,577
Why are you taking out your
anger at Urmila's words on me?

317
00:17:10,640 --> 00:17:11,920
Do one thing, meet Das and

318
00:17:11,956 --> 00:17:13,930
find out how many people
have a problem with him.

319
00:17:14,363 --> 00:17:16,151
I am sure that must
be a very long list.

320
00:17:16,200 --> 00:17:17,869
Every single girl in
Lonpur must be on it.

321
00:17:17,923 --> 00:17:20,457
Hey, don't speculate.
Just go and do your job.

322
00:17:20,630 --> 00:17:22,097
I need to speak to Henry.

323
00:17:22,863 --> 00:17:24,357
Yes partner!

324
00:17:32,190 --> 00:17:33,663
Oh Henry.

325
00:17:34,730 --> 00:17:36,997
Stop going to girls with
my marriage proposal!

326
00:17:37,080 --> 00:17:39,403
-But she is beautiful, right?
-I don't care Henry!

327
00:17:40,543 --> 00:17:42,330
So do you want to be like Das?

328
00:17:42,803 --> 00:17:45,583
When you're old we will find you
with a newspaper in your hand.

329
00:17:46,597 --> 00:17:50,783
You too! Duffers! Both of you.
Big duffers.

330
00:17:51,217 --> 00:17:52,570
What happened now?

331
00:17:59,077 --> 00:18:00,663
What?

332
00:18:01,760 --> 00:18:03,306
What are you doing?

333
00:18:03,977 --> 00:18:05,603
Nothing. What did Das say?

334
00:18:07,597 --> 00:18:12,263
That guy is still stuck on
Bhootnath and Menaka.

335
00:18:12,657 --> 00:18:15,450
He says he has no
enemies in Lonpur.

336
00:18:16,137 --> 00:18:18,017
And everyone in the
city knows everyone else.

337
00:18:18,517 --> 00:18:21,163
So Sanyal is definitely
not from around here.

338
00:18:22,137 --> 00:18:23,650
But now the question is,

339
00:18:23,683 --> 00:18:27,590
which person from Lonpur
gave Sanyal Das' details?

340
00:18:28,403 --> 00:18:31,017
Do you know how many drunkards
we have who gossip all day?

341
00:18:31,880 --> 00:18:34,360
Buggers like Chatterjee
do that all day!

342
00:18:40,170 --> 00:18:41,550
What?

343
00:18:42,637 --> 00:18:44,183
Shekhar! Shekhar! Ah!

344
00:18:46,610 --> 00:18:47,983
Shekhar!

345
00:18:49,777 --> 00:18:50,863
What the hell?

346
00:18:51,143 --> 00:18:52,909
I sent you to Das didn't I?

347
00:18:53,136 --> 00:18:54,470
Where else did you go?

348
00:18:54,877 --> 00:18:56,437
I just came from his shop.

349
00:19:00,383 --> 00:19:01,570
Hey Shekhar!

350
00:19:02,130 --> 00:19:03,210
Shekhar!

351
00:19:06,783 --> 00:19:08,990
What happened Shekhar?

352
00:19:12,103 --> 00:19:13,643
Where are you going?

353
00:19:26,197 --> 00:19:27,983
Shekhar! I am heading back.

354
00:19:34,743 --> 00:19:36,163
Hey!

355
00:19:42,983 --> 00:19:44,217
How is this open?

356
00:19:44,757 --> 00:19:46,297
Let's go and inform Das.

357
00:19:50,450 --> 00:19:51,717
What are you doing?

358
00:19:55,870 --> 00:19:57,803
What? Me?

359
00:19:58,400 --> 00:19:59,940
Do I look like a wrestler to you?

360
00:20:00,400 --> 00:20:02,167
Come on soldier. You can do it.
Come on.

361
00:20:02,388 --> 00:20:04,629
It's not that easy
to remove a grill...

362
00:20:09,850 --> 00:20:12,117
Hey... Shekhar,
this is trespassing.

363
00:20:23,720 --> 00:20:25,066
What are we doing here?

364
00:20:25,870 --> 00:20:27,083
Tell me?

365
00:20:48,170 --> 00:20:49,297
Interesting.

366
00:20:50,230 --> 00:20:52,510
Did we break in
here to look at art?

367
00:20:53,010 --> 00:20:54,057
Let's take this with us.

368
00:20:54,920 --> 00:20:56,406
Have you lost your mind?

369
00:20:56,470 --> 00:20:58,783
We are already here anyway.
Let's take it with us.

370
00:20:59,437 --> 00:21:01,277
Help? Help?
Please, come on help.

371
00:21:01,550 --> 00:21:03,050
-Shekhar...
-Come on, lift.

372
00:21:05,010 --> 00:21:06,177
What?

373
00:21:07,810 --> 00:21:09,070
What is this?

374
00:21:10,350 --> 00:21:13,823
[in Bengali] On the lap of the
banyan tree, go towards the South,

375
00:21:14,237 --> 00:21:16,310
then towards North east,

376
00:21:18,050 --> 00:21:20,090
I give you the directions!

377
00:21:24,203 --> 00:21:25,617
This is a long tunnel.

378
00:21:29,023 --> 00:21:30,277
What?

379
00:21:30,760 --> 00:21:32,589
Everyone should have
an assistant like you.

380
00:21:32,617 --> 00:21:34,910
Hey! I am not your assistant,
I am your partner okay?

381
00:21:36,837 --> 00:21:39,096
Shekhar where are you going? Hey.

382
00:21:46,010 --> 00:21:48,637
I feel like sneezing.
What if I fall?

383
00:21:51,043 --> 00:21:52,737
You will stop sneezing for good.

384
00:22:13,623 --> 00:22:15,603
Oh God... where are we?

385
00:22:16,803 --> 00:22:18,943
This is the vault of
Lonpur Co-operative Bank.

386
00:22:35,943 --> 00:22:39,270
A truck of cash
arrives every Saturday.

387
00:22:39,900 --> 00:22:42,064
That is how they must have
planned their robbery.

388
00:22:42,064 --> 00:22:44,990
Commit the robbery on Saturday night
since the bank will be closed on Sunday.

389
00:22:45,030 --> 00:22:47,570
By the time the bank opens on
Monday morning they would be gone.

390
00:22:48,170 --> 00:22:49,303
Right? Shekhar?

391
00:22:50,683 --> 00:22:54,056
Shekhar, this robbery was carried
out on the weekend on purpose.

392
00:22:54,123 --> 00:22:55,357
-Cellotape.
-Cellotape?

393
00:22:55,560 --> 00:22:57,880
Banatul Industrial Detergent.

394
00:22:57,915 --> 00:23:00,062
You won't find it
anywhere near Lonpur.

395
00:23:01,563 --> 00:23:05,517
Ladies and gentlemen, now with
extra foam and hydrogen peroxide.

396
00:23:05,542 --> 00:23:08,070
-Hydrogen peroxide?
-Ding!

397
00:23:12,103 --> 00:23:16,629
Did you pass by Das' shop
day before yesterday?

398
00:23:18,190 --> 00:23:20,643
Yes, I passed by
this place on my walk.

399
00:23:22,057 --> 00:23:23,923
I could smell something too.

400
00:23:24,703 --> 00:23:26,130
Like something was burning!

401
00:23:26,210 --> 00:23:29,583
Nitro... Nitroglycerin.
Nitroglycerin.

402
00:23:29,750 --> 00:23:31,103
It is used in bombs.

403
00:23:32,257 --> 00:23:34,103
And as soon as you come in
contact with it

404
00:23:34,920 --> 00:23:36,787
a person will start sneezing.

405
00:23:37,023 --> 00:23:38,463
-Shekhar!
-Hey, are you crazy?

406
00:23:38,535 --> 00:23:39,810
He is a genius!

407
00:23:46,280 --> 00:23:47,654
Hey! What are you doing?

408
00:23:48,137 --> 00:23:50,370
-Hey!
-Don't worry I will take care of it.

409
00:23:54,360 --> 00:23:56,694
What are you doing Shekhar?

410
00:23:56,830 --> 00:23:58,590
I was just calling you a genius.

411
00:24:09,583 --> 00:24:10,797
Now do you know who did it?

412
00:24:11,090 --> 00:24:12,730
Just by looking at the masks?

413
00:24:13,970 --> 00:24:15,583
You just called me a genius, right?

414
00:24:20,017 --> 00:24:22,290
Why did you call me here?

415
00:24:22,910 --> 00:24:24,670
-To tell you a story.
-What do you mean?

416
00:24:24,890 --> 00:24:28,417
I mean, this story has
drama, emotion, romance

417
00:24:29,837 --> 00:24:31,677
and even action.

418
00:24:32,163 --> 00:24:33,790
But it is still a crime.

419
00:24:34,470 --> 00:24:37,830
You see, a few months ago some
people got together and made a plan.

420
00:24:38,560 --> 00:24:39,973
A plan to loot the bank.

421
00:24:40,177 --> 00:24:42,063
But why are you telling us this?

422
00:24:42,120 --> 00:24:43,689
Because there is a list...

423
00:24:45,800 --> 00:24:48,000
Laha! File!

424
00:24:52,880 --> 00:24:56,163
This is a list of all the loans that
were rejected in the last six months.

425
00:24:57,160 --> 00:24:58,460
Bhootnath!

426
00:24:59,670 --> 00:25:00,997
Goswami.

427
00:25:01,983 --> 00:25:03,123
Chatterjee.

428
00:25:06,317 --> 00:25:07,590
Miss Urmila.

429
00:25:09,097 --> 00:25:10,210
'U' for Urmila.

430
00:25:10,235 --> 00:25:13,008
Yes, 'U' for Urmila and
'C' for Chatterjee.

431
00:25:13,408 --> 00:25:14,575
You see what I see?

432
00:25:15,520 --> 00:25:16,620
Yes...

433
00:25:17,197 --> 00:25:20,163
They had a plan to build
a home away from Lonpur.

434
00:25:20,217 --> 00:25:22,237
They needed a loan and
it was rejected.

435
00:25:22,280 --> 00:25:26,000
Primary applicant Chatterjee.
Co-applicant Urmila.

436
00:25:26,950 --> 00:25:31,090
And when the bank refused they
decided to loot the bank itself.

437
00:25:31,115 --> 00:25:33,030
Wait... wait... wait a second sir.

438
00:25:33,577 --> 00:25:35,527
The two of us are
in a relationship...

439
00:25:35,723 --> 00:25:37,023
everyone knows that by now.

440
00:25:37,057 --> 00:25:39,783
I accept it, but I didn't
loot any banks!

441
00:25:39,997 --> 00:25:43,063
I didn't even know about the
secret tunnel under Das' shop.

442
00:25:43,197 --> 00:25:45,557
You didn't know but she knew.

443
00:25:45,790 --> 00:25:46,930
Knew what?

444
00:25:48,003 --> 00:25:49,623
I don't know anything.

445
00:25:50,397 --> 00:25:53,377
You sign on the receipts at
your medical shop don't you?

446
00:25:54,024 --> 00:25:54,990
Yes.

447
00:25:55,037 --> 00:25:58,490
You know the register at
the Lonpur library?

448
00:25:58,680 --> 00:26:00,222
It has your sign.

449
00:26:00,303 --> 00:26:03,977
You borrowed the book with the
blueprint didn't you?

450
00:26:05,437 --> 00:26:09,137
Which had a map to the tunnel
below the bank, right?

451
00:26:09,720 --> 00:26:13,187
I... cross-checked that signature

452
00:26:13,680 --> 00:26:14,966
and it was a perfect match.

453
00:26:15,303 --> 00:26:17,557
Just like you and Chatterjee.

454
00:26:18,610 --> 00:26:20,677
Then he must have done that.

455
00:26:20,963 --> 00:26:22,512
Yes, to get me out of the way.

456
00:26:22,537 --> 00:26:24,237
Sir, you see!
She is talking too much!

457
00:26:24,330 --> 00:26:27,844
Talking too much? You stole the
money to go back to your wife, right?

458
00:26:27,844 --> 00:26:29,530
-You bloody cheater.
-Hey! Not a cheater.

459
00:26:30,083 --> 00:26:31,243
No cheater.

460
00:26:31,570 --> 00:26:33,203
Cheater is an American distortion.

461
00:26:33,630 --> 00:26:34,923
The word is cheat.

462
00:26:34,923 --> 00:26:37,203
British English?
Do you work for the BBC?

463
00:26:37,240 --> 00:26:38,917
Oh no, thank you very much.

464
00:26:40,497 --> 00:26:43,710
-You are a cheat! Yes, you are.
-I am a cheat?

465
00:26:43,837 --> 00:26:48,295
She is a selfish woman. I was about
to leave my caring wife for you!

466
00:26:48,320 --> 00:26:52,040
-Caring wife? You just remembered that?
-Quiet. Calm down.

467
00:26:52,075 --> 00:26:53,903
Shut up!

468
00:26:53,990 --> 00:26:55,137
Both of you shut up.

469
00:26:55,370 --> 00:26:56,517
Ananto!

470
00:26:56,623 --> 00:26:58,450
Ananto! Hey!

471
00:26:59,603 --> 00:27:01,537
Listen, head to their
houses right now...

472
00:27:01,562 --> 00:27:03,777
-Sir--
-Shut up! Shut up. Go to their house...

473
00:27:03,970 --> 00:27:06,630
...search their house, they must
be hiding the money there.

474
00:27:06,663 --> 00:27:08,557
Find the money, count
it and bring it back here.

475
00:27:08,563 --> 00:27:09,937
Hey, Ananto.

476
00:27:10,510 --> 00:27:14,757
36 Lakhs 57 thousand and 19 rupees.
And 75 paise.

477
00:27:15,803 --> 00:27:17,083
Go. Hurry up.

478
00:27:17,108 --> 00:27:20,710
-You stole so much money?
-Hey, hey, enough. Shut up!

479
00:27:21,063 --> 00:27:23,603
Look, the honeymoon
hotel is ready for you guys.

480
00:27:23,883 --> 00:27:26,563
-Tell me if you want to go in.
-Take your wife with you!

481
00:27:26,730 --> 00:27:28,543
-Sir--
-Shut up!

482
00:27:31,477 --> 00:27:34,303
Look, the two of you can leave.

483
00:27:34,883 --> 00:27:36,030
But... But...

484
00:27:36,530 --> 00:27:38,463
the investigation is
not over yet, okay?

485
00:27:38,937 --> 00:27:41,843
Don't talk to anyone about this.
And if you do, he won't spare you.

486
00:27:48,657 --> 00:27:50,090
-Sir...
-Shut up!

487
00:28:00,790 --> 00:28:03,883
Hello? Hello Shekhar? We found
the real thieves and the money.

488
00:28:04,320 --> 00:28:08,226
Why are you so excited?
Did you think I could be wrong?

489
00:28:08,470 --> 00:28:11,111
Fine Shekhar. We found
the money and the thieves

490
00:28:11,135 --> 00:28:12,590
just like you said, okay?

491
00:28:25,443 --> 00:28:27,117
Hello Mr. Sanyal.

492
00:28:37,470 --> 00:28:38,770
Mr. Goswami.

493
00:28:40,143 --> 00:28:42,777
It was a good plan but
you made a mistake.

494
00:28:43,617 --> 00:28:48,257
36 Lakhs 57 thousand and 19 rupees.
And 75 paise.

495
00:28:48,663 --> 00:28:51,737
I said the wrong amount
at the police station Mr. Goswami.

496
00:28:52,310 --> 00:28:54,670
So that you could take
us to uncle Abra.

497
00:29:03,400 --> 00:29:04,907
PAHARPUR 2 KMs

498
00:29:15,877 --> 00:29:18,350
-What did you do uncle?
-What?

499
00:29:18,383 --> 00:29:21,803
You said that you found
28 lakh 95 thousand rupees.

500
00:29:21,850 --> 00:29:24,455
But 36 lakhs are
missing from the bank!

501
00:29:24,480 --> 00:29:29,480
Here! Take this 8 lakhs and this
36 lakhs and count it yourself!

502
00:29:29,508 --> 00:29:32,403
Obviously I will count it myself.

503
00:29:36,170 --> 00:29:38,130
When did you get this idea?

504
00:29:40,423 --> 00:29:44,317
I came to Lonpur to search for
something in Mangal Ashram.

505
00:29:44,342 --> 00:29:46,310
As Mrs. H calls it... Lady Luck.

506
00:29:46,917 --> 00:29:48,643
She is the one who
saved Bablu's life today.

507
00:29:48,863 --> 00:29:49,943
Otherwise...

508
00:29:50,123 --> 00:29:52,903
In real life I don't have a
lady nor do I have any luck.

509
00:29:53,177 --> 00:29:55,177
Das... don't be sad.

510
00:29:55,423 --> 00:29:57,023
You will find her soon enough.

511
00:29:57,690 --> 00:29:58,803
When?

512
00:29:59,170 --> 00:30:00,963
I am tired of looking.

513
00:30:03,237 --> 00:30:04,431
Mr. Das,

514
00:30:04,431 --> 00:30:07,614
if not today, you will find her
tomorrow - your dream girl.

515
00:30:08,143 --> 00:30:10,050
Very soon you will have a lady

516
00:30:10,757 --> 00:30:12,437
and luck on your side.

517
00:30:13,003 --> 00:30:14,057
Really?

518
00:30:17,123 --> 00:30:19,983
You are my closest friend Goswami.

519
00:30:22,450 --> 00:30:25,863
After the landlords only you
could make use of that tunnel.

520
00:30:28,137 --> 00:30:29,563
Urmila's sign...

521
00:30:30,303 --> 00:30:32,457
the one you made in the register.

522
00:30:35,720 --> 00:30:36,960
It was easy.

523
00:30:37,016 --> 00:30:39,609
She used to sign on the bills

524
00:30:39,997 --> 00:30:41,317
and I just copied it.

525
00:30:41,710 --> 00:30:43,517
When it was time
to execute the plan

526
00:30:44,610 --> 00:30:46,830
your uncle Abra entered the scene.

527
00:30:49,523 --> 00:30:52,770
Nobody in Lonpur knew him
and there were no police records.

528
00:30:53,037 --> 00:30:54,117
Smart move.

529
00:30:55,683 --> 00:30:57,030
But you made a mistake.

530
00:30:58,550 --> 00:31:01,197
You made him a guarantor
on your loan application.

531
00:31:03,397 --> 00:31:06,163
He turned into Sanyal to turn
Das into Devdas.

532
00:31:06,188 --> 00:31:08,090
The poor guy didn't get
his Chandramukhi,

533
00:31:08,400 --> 00:31:10,473
nor Paro, nor Menaka.

534
00:31:13,050 --> 00:31:14,297
Bomb.

535
00:31:16,043 --> 00:31:18,450
You made it well.
Silent. Powerful.

536
00:31:19,770 --> 00:31:21,383
But you made a mistake there too.

537
00:31:22,423 --> 00:31:24,123
The smell of nitroglycerin.

538
00:31:27,930 --> 00:31:30,750
If I hadn't smelt it I could
never have found out.

539
00:31:32,510 --> 00:31:35,323
I should have used ammonium nitrate
that was my mistake.

540
00:31:36,090 --> 00:31:37,697
Ammonium perchlorate.

541
00:31:39,243 --> 00:31:41,803
Why don't you make
the bomb next time?

542
00:31:44,543 --> 00:31:45,509
Seriously?

543
00:31:45,534 --> 00:31:47,430
We can share the money.

544
00:31:47,863 --> 00:31:48,866
No... I mean...

545
00:31:48,890 --> 00:31:51,923
my company does want me to hit
certain money targets though.

546
00:31:54,237 --> 00:31:55,977
Well, anyway...

547
00:31:57,177 --> 00:32:00,517
it's clear how and why this
robbery took place.

548
00:32:00,783 --> 00:32:01,816
Is it clear?

549
00:32:01,843 --> 00:32:05,830
Yes, I mean... anyone could have
signed there right?

550
00:32:06,490 --> 00:32:09,870
So how did these two...

551
00:32:18,083 --> 00:32:19,376
Medrol.

552
00:32:19,560 --> 00:32:21,480
Give this to Abra uncle.

553
00:32:24,803 --> 00:32:28,643
Medrol means that uncle has COPD.

554
00:32:29,023 --> 00:32:30,423
Hey, do that later.

555
00:32:30,910 --> 00:32:33,377
Let him cough. He has COPD.

556
00:32:34,037 --> 00:32:36,163
Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease.

557
00:32:36,323 --> 00:32:38,089
Chronic... Pul...

558
00:32:38,123 --> 00:32:40,943
Yes, exactly.

559
00:32:42,537 --> 00:32:45,283
Laha, you remember the masks
we found in the trash?

560
00:32:46,337 --> 00:32:49,510
One of those masks had an
extra layer of cloth.

561
00:32:49,780 --> 00:32:51,534
You see, digging
a tunnel with bombs

562
00:32:51,760 --> 00:32:53,550
causes a lot of sand
and dirt to float around.

563
00:32:53,749 --> 00:32:55,469
That would have triggered his COPD.

564
00:32:56,003 --> 00:32:57,650
This was for uncle's protection.

565
00:32:58,210 --> 00:32:59,350
Uncle?

566
00:33:00,303 --> 00:33:01,817
You see your nephew here?

567
00:33:02,910 --> 00:33:04,117
He is very cunning.

568
00:33:05,623 --> 00:33:09,023
He was sitting in Khasha Blanca
when the crime was committed.

569
00:33:10,083 --> 00:33:11,743
He has an alibi.

570
00:33:12,837 --> 00:33:14,370
Far away from the crime scene.

571
00:33:16,389 --> 00:33:19,542
Catching him without the loot
was pointless.

572
00:33:20,663 --> 00:33:23,763
That is why we caught
him here red-handed.

573
00:33:29,910 --> 00:33:31,123
Thank you Shekhar.

574
00:33:31,197 --> 00:33:34,477
This is a very big case that has been
added to Lonpur Police Station's ledger.

575
00:33:35,217 --> 00:33:37,423
Yes, but this time a
thank you won't be enough.

576
00:33:37,950 --> 00:33:40,077
Okay, well would you like
rasgullas or mutton?

577
00:33:40,463 --> 00:33:43,155
No way. There is a
big reward and a credit.

578
00:33:43,479 --> 00:33:45,076
We want a share in both.

579
00:33:45,550 --> 00:33:48,650
But Shekhar... what
about our arrangement?

580
00:33:50,050 --> 00:33:52,137
That is over now.
This will now be my department.

581
00:33:52,943 --> 00:33:54,217
Shekhar?

582
00:33:55,050 --> 00:33:56,430
Don't talk to me.

583
00:33:57,270 --> 00:33:59,377
-What?
-Discuss it with the corporate guy.

584
00:34:00,800 --> 00:34:02,027
Doctor?

585
00:34:10,297 --> 00:34:11,350
Yes, this...

586
00:34:11,750 --> 00:34:14,143
this is your certificate.

587
00:34:16,410 --> 00:34:18,410
And cash?

588
00:34:19,040 --> 00:34:21,073
Yes, here... 15,000...

589
00:34:25,683 --> 00:34:28,903
Two years of rent,
the bulb you broke

590
00:34:29,640 --> 00:34:31,113
and all other damages.

591
00:35:13,840 --> 00:35:15,980
We are ready to
move on to stage two.

